  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Multisectoral Assistance to Vulnerable Populations in North Kivu and Ituri and Support for Durable Solutions for Displaced Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) continues to experience armed and intercommunal conflicts, disasters related to natural hazards and disease epidemics that have created one of the world&#x2019;s most complex and long-standing crises. Since October 2022, North Kivu province has been affected by the resumption of activism by the M23 armed group, leading to a severe security and humanitarian crisis. As of the beginning of 2023, the group has extended its control over additional territories, further exacerbating the humanitarian situation in and around the North Kivu province, causing mass displacement of almost half a million internally displaced persons (IDPs) currently settled in spontaneous sites and collective centres in and around Goma. IOM is providing emergency multi-sectoral assistance to populations affected by the M23 crisis, particularly in areas less covered by the current response, in Djugu and Mahagi territories of Ituri province, where urgent and significant humanitarian needs are largely underfunded. Specifically, IOM is strengthening the management of displacement sites in coordination with local communities, conducting assessments using the Displacement Tracking Matrix Return Index to evaluate conditions in places of origin to inform durable solutions for displaced populations, and providing mental health and psychosocial support to displaced populations.</narrative>
  </description>
